From 12186a33504ca94311269637f90836b8e9b3fec2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:17:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] skbuff: preserve MAC header length in page-pool copies

Generic XDP can replace an skb with a page-pool copy when a program has
BPF_F_XDP_HAS_FRAGS. skb_copy_header() does not copy mac_len. A subsequent
CPUMAP redirect therefore pulls zero bytes from the replacement skb,
leaving its Ethernet header at the IP receive boundary. Loopback UDP
reaches TC on the selected CPU, then is dropped with IP_INHDR; TCP, SCTP
and MPTCP connection setup fails on the same path.

Copy mac_len alongside the skb header. The non-frags generic path does
not use this copy, and native CPUMAP construction remains unchanged.
The composition selftests in this series cover real IPv4/IPv6 UDP with
and without the frags program flag. The external policy also exercises
TCP, SCTP and MPTCP through this path.

Fixes: e6d5dbdd20aa ("xdp: add multi-buff support for xdp running in generic mode")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 net/core/skbuff.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/core/skbuff.c b/net/core/skbuff.c
index cc3b4b70288b..e2a61cea2602 100644
--- a/net/core/skbuff.c
+++ b/net/core/skbuff.c
@@ -966,6 +966,8 @@ int skb_pp_cow_data(struct page_pool *pool, struct sk_buff **pskb,
 
 	skb_reserve(nskb, headroom);
 	skb_copy_header(nskb, skb);
+	/* Generic XDP redirect uses this to remove the copied MAC header. */
+	nskb->mac_len = skb->mac_len;
 	skb_mark_for_recycle(nskb);
 
 	err = skb_copy_bits(skb, 0, nskb->data, size);
